{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"9a05acff2407ddce","name":"card_event_eastern_front","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/events/card_event_eastern_front","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EASTERN FRONT BOUND","text":"Give your Alpine units +1+1. Draw an Alpine unit from your deck.","flavorText":"After the German invasion of the Soviet Union, Mussolini decided to show solidarity with his German ally by sending Italian troops to fight on the Eastern Front. From 1941 to 1943 the Italian Royal Army maintained two army units on the Eastern Front, the Italian Expeditionary Corps in Russia (Corpo di Spedizione Italiano in Russia, or CSIR) and the Italian 8th Army. In total the Italians maintained 3 corps on the Eastern front, a total of 229,000 men, 22,000 vehicles, and 1,340 artillery pieces. Many of the Italian troops were Alpini mountain troops, and although they were elite troops they lacked experience and equipment to fight on the vast and flat Russian steps. By the end of February 1943 about 30,000 Italians had been killed and another 54,000 would later die in captivity.","faction":"Italy","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_eastern_front","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_eastern_front_title","SourceString":"EASTERN FRONT BOUND","LocalizedString":"EASTERN FRONT BOUND"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_eastern_front_text","SourceString":"Give your Alpine units +1+1. Draw an Alpine unit from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Give your Alpine units +1+1. Draw an Alpine unit from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_eastern_front_history","SourceString":"After the German invasion of the Soviet Union, Mussolini decided to show solidarity with his German ally by sending Italian troops to fight on the Eastern Front. From 1941 to 1943 the Italian Royal Army maintained two army units on the Eastern Front, the Italian Expeditionary Corps in Russia (Corpo di Spedizione Italiano in Russia, or CSIR) and the Italian 8th Army. In total the Italians maintained 3 corps on the Eastern front, a total of 229,000 men, 22,000 vehicles, and 1,340 artillery pieces. Many of the Italian troops were Alpini mountain troops, and although they were elite troops they lacked experience and equipment to fight on the vast and flat Russian steps. By the end of February 1943 about 30,000 Italians had been killed and another 54,000 would later die in captivity.","LocalizedString":"After the German invasion of the Soviet Union, Mussolini decided to show solidarity with his German ally by sending Italian troops to fight on the Eastern Front. From 1941 to 1943 the Italian Royal Army maintained two army units on the Eastern Front, the Italian Expeditionary Corps in Russia (Corpo di Spedizione Italiano in Russia, or CSIR) and the Italian 8th Army. In total the Italians maintained 3 corps on the Eastern front, a total of 229,000 men, 22,000 vehicles, and 1,340 artillery pieces. Many of the Italian troops were Alpini mountain troops, and although they were elite troops they lacked experience and equipment to fight on the vast and flat Russian steps. By the end of February 1943 about 30,000 Italians had been killed and another 54,000 would later die in captivity."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Alpine"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Organic_War_Drums_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Organic_War_Drums_2.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/02_Allegiance/T_eastern_front_bound.T_eastern_front_bound","SubPathString":""},"artist":"WWII Propaganda Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/As